        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can you jump-start my car at the roadside?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>In most cases, yes, if the battery is simply flat rather than faulty. We'll attempt a jump start on the spot, and if that gets you going again there's no need for a tow.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What if you can't fix the problem on the spot?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>If the fault can't be resolved at the roadside — for example the battery won't hold charge, or the tyre can't be safely changed — we'll move straight into breakdown recovery and take the vehicle to a garage or your chosen destination.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you carry fuel for cars that have run out?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>We can bring a small amount of the right fuel to get you to the nearest fuel station. Tell us the fuel type your vehicle takes when you call so we bring the correct one.</p>
          </details>
